# Leave this unset. Local dev (Vite proxy), the docker-compose/nginx setup,
# and the Vercel deployment (via vercel.json rewrites) all make the frontend
# and backend same-origin from the browser's perspective, so relative '/api'
# and '/uploads' paths already work everywhere.
#
# Only set VITE_BACKEND_URL if you deploy the frontend somewhere that can't
# proxy /api/* itself, so the browser must call the backend's own domain
# directly. Cross-origin cookies are unreliable this way — Safari blocks
# third-party cookies by default, and Chrome increasingly does too, so the
# httpOnly auth cookies this app relies on may simply not be stored. Prefer
# a same-origin proxy (see vercel.json) over this whenever you have the
# option. Vite bakes this in at BUILD time if you do set it.
VITE_BACKEND_URL=
